abstract: "Article/clause/point-level knowledge graph of Vietnamese civil law
  (20 corpus laws, 13,151 chunks, entity and relation layers) with validity
  intervals, verified amendment and succession edges, and a stratified temporal
  QA benchmark of 716 published questions in four audited cohorts: 281 core
  (12 hand-authored, 269 generated), 106 extension round 1, 64 extension
  round 2 from the 1996-2015 statute era, and 265 round-3 scale-up items,
  plus a publicly quarantined pool of 542 rejected candidates. All gold labels
  carry multi-round adjudication
  trails; no question remains in an unverifiable state. On the core set,
  temporal-consistency retrieval raises Qwen2.5-3B citation accuracy from
  0.488 to 0.601 (McNemar p = 5.8e-05) and retrieval Hit@5 to 0.811.
  Reference paper: docs/report/ViCivil-TKG_paper_en.pdf (English
  edition; the Vietnamese edition is archived)."
